# HOW TO EDIT THIS FILE:
# The "handy ruler" below makes it easier to edit a package description.
# Line up the first '|' above the ':' following the base package name, and
# the '|' on the right side marks the last column you can put a character in.
# You must make exactly 11 lines for the formatting to be correct.  It's also
# customary to leave one space after the ':' except on otherwise blank lines.

         |-----handy-ruler------------------------------------------------------|
docker-engine: docker-engine (Docker Engine daemon)
docker-engine:
docker-engine: dockerd is the Docker daemon, the core of the Docker container
docker-engine: platform. It manages containers, images, networks and volumes
docker-engine: using the containerd and runc runtimes, and exposes a stable
docker-engine: REST API and the Docker Unix socket.
docker-engine:
docker-engine: This package is built from the official moby sources for
docker-engine: Slackware 15.0 (no systemd). It includes dockerd, docker-proxy
docker-engine: and docker-init (tini).
docker-engine:
docker-engine: Home: https://www.docker.com/ (moby https://github.com/moby/moby)